odule names and parameters as specified. No adding or omitting tasks, just exactly what\'s provided.\n\nPotential issues I might face:\n\n- Variable paths: Making sure the variables like vault_prerequisites and vault_installation_method are correctly referenced.\n- Ensuring that the import_tasks and include_tasks are used appropriately, especially for dynamic task inclusion.\n- Correctly handling the conditional tasks for Vault service enabling based on the vault_type variable.\n\nI should also check that the YAML syntax is correct, using proper indentation and no trailing spaces. Since it\'s for an Ansible Role, I must structure it correctly without any playbook-level directives.\n\nIn summary, I\'ll structure each task in order, use the correct modules and variables, ensure proper YAML formatting, and make sure the playbook starts with \'---\' and is self-contained as a role task list.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml file\n  include_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n    changed_when: false\n  run_once: true\n  delegate_to: localhost\n\n- name: Install prerequisites\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ vault_prerequisites }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Include installation method specific tasks\n  include_tasks: "{{ item }}"\n  with_items: "{{ vault_installation_method }}"\n\n- name: Add Vault environment variables\n  template:\n    src: vault.env.j2\n    dest: /etc/vault.d/vault.env\n    owner: vault\n    group: vault\n    mode: 0644\n  vars:\n    vault_env_settings: "{{ vault_environment_settings }}"\n  notify: Restart Vault service\n\n- name: Include hardening tasks\n  import_tasks: hardening.yml\n\n- name: Start and enable vault on OSS\n  systemd:\n    name: vault\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  when: vault_type == "oss"\n\n- name: Enable vault (non-OSS)\n  systemd:\n    name: vault\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  when: vault_type != "oss"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-1