d_unrestricted | default(false)` with a space around the pipe to indicate it\'s a filter.\n\nAdditionally, for the line length issues, I can split the long lines by using a list or the | operator for multi-line strings.\n\nSo, for each task where the line is too long, I\'ll split the line into multiple lines using | and proper indentation.\n\nNow, let me go through each task:\n\nTask 1: No issues.\n\nTask 2: The when clause is `grub_efi.stat.exists`, which is correct. No changes needed.\n\nTask 3: No issues.\n\nTask 4: The line parameter is long. I\'ll split it using |.\n\nTask 5: Similarly, split the line.\n\nTask 6: The when clause is `grub_password_unrestricted|default(false)`. I\'ll add a space around the | to make it `grub_password_unrestricted | default(false)`. Also, the replace string is long, so I\'ll split it using |.\n\nNow, applying these changes:\n\n- For Task 4 and Task 5, I\'ll split the line into multiple lines using |.\n- For Task 6, I\'ll adjust the when clause and split the replace string.\n\nI\'ll ensure that all changes maintain the original functionality and only fix the yamllint issues.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Get the path to the efi variables directory\n  ansible.builtin.stat:\n    path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/\n  register: grub_efi\n\n- name: Remove the grub.cfg file on EFI systems\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /boot/grub2/grub.cfg\n    state: absent\n  when: grub_efi.stat.exists\n\n- name: Install a user template for grub\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: 01_users.j2\n    dest: /etc/grub.d/01_users\n    mode: 0644\n    owner: root\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Add password to the grub configuration on EFI systems\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2-efi.cfg\n    line: |\n      set superusers = \'{{ grub_password_user }}\'\n      password_pbkdf2 {{ grub_password_hash }} grub_password_user 8 100000 32\n    insertafter: EOF\n    create: yes\n  when: grub_efi.stat.exists\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Add password to the grub configuration on MBR systems\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2.cfg\n    line: |\n      set superusers = \'{{ grub_password_user }}\'\n      password_pbkdf2 {{ grub_password_hash }} grub_password_user 8 100000 32\n    insertafter: EOF\n    create: yes\n  when: grub_efi.stat.exists\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Modify the grub configuration to allow unrestricted access\n  ansible.builtin.replace:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    regexp: \'^\\s*#\\\\s*DO\\\\s*NOT\\\\s*EDIT\\\\s*THIS\\\\s*FILE!$\'\n    replace: |\n      set superusers = \'{{ grub_password_user }}\'\n      password_pbkdf2 {{ grub_password_hash }} grub_password_user 8 100000 32\n    with_verbosity: 2\n  loop: "{{ grub_password_unrestricted | default(false) ? grub_password_unrestricted_files : [] }}"\n  when: grub_password_unrestricted | default(false)\n  notify: Update grub\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T08:43:26.576368944Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 38461261645, 'load_duration': 83933852, 'prompt_eval_count': 1296, 'prompt_eval_duration': 552249679, 'eval_count': 1691, 'eval_duration': 37824588519, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--a0572b4b-b57d-4cac-8957-933ee541a3b4-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1296, 'output_tokens': 1691, 'total_tokens': 2987}
