er Ansible facts without becoming root. I\'ll use the setup module with become set to false.\n\nTask 5 installs packages from bootstrap_facts_packages. I\'ll use the package module in a loop, setting become to the value of bootstrap_become.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks are in the correct order as specified. Also, each task should have the exact names and modules as provided. I\'ll avoid adding any extra comments or explanations since the user emphasized only the YAML playbook should be output.\n\nLet me double-check each task for correct module names, parameters, and conditions. Ensuring that variables like bootstrap_timeout and bootstrap_wait_for_host are correctly referenced.\n\nFinally, I\'ll structure the YAML, making sure each task is properly indented and that the playbook starts with \'---\' followed by a linebreak. I\'ll review the entire playbook to confirm it adheres to all the given instructions without any omissions or modifications.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  loop: true\n\n- wait_for_port:\n    port: \'{{ bootstrap_port }}\'\n    timeout: \'{{ bootstrap_timeout }}\'\n  when:\n    - ansible_connection is defined\n    - ansible_connection not in [\'container\', \'docker\', \'community.docker.docker\']\n    - bootstrap_wait_for_host\n  become: false\n\n- include_tasks: prepare_system.yml\n  become: yes\n\n- setup:\n  become: false\n\n- package:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ bootstrap_facts_packages | default([]) | list }}"\n  become: \'{{ bootstrap_become | default(false) }}\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T08:47:01.678640562Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12979903909, 'load_duration': 104277253, 'prompt_eval_count': 510, 'prompt_eval_duration': 105637666, 'eval_count': 746, 'eval_duration': 12769273716, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--402c6da2-bdb6-496d-9f8a-d138850