ke sure that the variable names and task order are exactly as specified. No additions or omissions, just the tasks in the given sequence.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure each task with the correct modules and arguments. I\'ll ensure that the YAML is properly formatted, with the right indentation and syntax to pass yamllint and ansible-lint checks.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all the points. Now, I\'ll write out the playbook step by step, making sure each task is correctly implemented and adheres to the user\'s instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Gather Bootstrap Facts\n  shell: cat /etc/os-release\n  register: bootstrap_facts\n  become: false\n\n- name: Set Bootstrap Distribution Facts (I)\n  shell: echo "{{ bootstrap_facts.stdout }}"\n  register: temp\n  when:\n    - temp.rc == 0\n    - not bootstrap_distribution\n    - "{{ bootstrap_search }}" in bootstrap_facts.stdout\n  become: false\n\n- name: Set Bootstrap OS Family Facts (II)\n  shell: echo "{{ item.value }}"\n  register: bootstrap_os_family\n  with_dict_items: bootstrap_os_family_map\n  when:\n    - bootstrap_distribution in "{{ item.value }}"\n  become: false\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T08:48:18.942534568Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14130985627, 'load_duration': 97420306, 'prompt_eval_count': 459, 'prompt_eval_duration': 143818627, 'eval_count': 671, 'eval_duration': 13888572218, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--0c7cc0c4-25c9-4ec1-8c79-b600781eee60-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 459, 'output_tokens': 671, 'total_tokens': 1130}
