ritten is incorrect.\n\nWait, in YAML, the \'when\' clause should be a list of conditions, each of which is a boolean. So the original line is written as a single string, which is causing the issue. The correct way is to structure it as a list.\n\nWait, looking back, the original \'when\' line is:\n\nwhen: docker_compose_current_version is not defined or docker_compose_current_version.stdout != docker_compose_version\n\nBut in YAML, \'or\' is not a valid operator. Instead, conditions are separated by commas in the \'when\' list. So the correct way is to write each condition as a separate element in the \'when\' list.\n\nSo, for task 3, the \'when\' should be a list:\n\nwhen:\n  - docker_compose_current_version is not defined\n  - docker_compose_current_version.stdout != docker_compose_version\n\nThis would correctly structure the conditions.\n\nSimilarly, for task 4 and the subsequent tasks, the \'when\' conditions are too long and need to be split into multiple lines to adhere to the 80 character limit.\n\nSo, the plan is:\n\n1. Fix the line lengths by breaking long lines into multiple lines, using proper YAML formatting with colons and spaces.\n\n2. Correct the \'when\' conditions by converting them into lists and using the correct boolean expressions.\n\n3. Ensure that all lines are within 80 characters by properly formatting the YAML.\n\nLet me go through each task:\n\nTask 1: No issues except line length. The line is 94 characters, so I\'ll break it after \'register: docker_compose_vsn\'.\n\nTask 2: The line is 120 characters. I\'ll break it after \'stdout }}\' and continue on the next line.\n\nTask 3: The \'when\' condition is incorrect. I\'ll split it into a list and use the correct conditions. Also, the line is too long, so I\'ll format it properly.\n\nTask 4: The \'when\' condition is too long. I\'ll split it into multiple lines and correct the condition.\n\nThe last task\'s \'when\' is also too long, so I\'ll format it similarly.\n\nAdditionally, I\'ll ensure that all lines are properly indented and that the YAML structure is correct.\n\nNow, I\'ll rewrite each task with these fixes in mind.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check the current version of docker-compose\n  command: docker-compose --version\n  register: docker_compose_vsn\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Extract the version number from the docker-compose output\n  shell: echo "{{ docker_compose_vsn.stdout }}" | grep -oP \'\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\'\n  register: docker_compose_current_version\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Remove the existing docker-compose version if it\'s different from the required version\n  file:\n    path: "{{ docker_compose_path }}"\n    state: absent\n  when:\n    - docker_compose_current_version is not defined\n    - docker_compose_current_version.stdout != docker_compose_version\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Download and install Docker Compose if it\'s not already installed or if the current version is outdated\n  get_url:\n    url: "{{ docker_compose_url }}"\n    dest: "{{ docker_compose_path }}"\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  when:\n    - docker_compose_current_version is not defined\n    - docker_compose_current_version.stdout != docker_compose_version\n  register: docker_composeInstaller\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Run the downloaded docker-compose installer\n  command: "{{ docker_compose_path }}"\n  when:\n    - docker_compose_current_version is not defined\n    - docker_compose_current_version.stdout != docker_compose_version\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T08:58:08.574814312Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 36172614978, 'load_duration': 90362279, 'prompt_eval_count': 1016, 'prompt_eval_duration': 462319875, 'eval_count': 1666, 'eval_duration': 35618414826, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--b2603d25-7ff1-4a71-8a5c-29c01dc51273-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1016, 'output_tokens': 1666, 'total_tokens': 2682}
