content='<think>\nAlright, I need to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions. Let me carefully go through each task and figure out how to structure the YAML.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the first line. That\'s straightforward. I\'ll make sure to include that.\n\nNext, each task has specific requirements. Let\'s list them out:\n\n1. Import assert.yml and run it once on localhost.\n   - I remember that in Ansible, importing tasks is done with the import_tasks module. Since it\'s for localhost, I\'ll set the host to localhost.\n\n2. Install the mysql package.\n   - Using apt for package management, I\'ll need to update the cache first and then install the mysql package. So I\'ll create a shell task that runs apt-get update and then installs mysql.\n\n3. Configure the mysql server.\n   - This involves creating a config file. I\'ll use the file module to create the .cnf file. The content will be a YAML list, which I can join with newlines. The options come from the mysql_configuration_options variable.\n\n4. Configure the mysql client.\n   - Similar to the server, but the file is named differently and only includes the socket option. Again, using the file module.\n\n5. Initialize the mysql service.\n   - For Alpine or Archlinux, I\'ll use a shell command. I\'ll check the OS with ansible_os_family and run the initialize command if it\'s either.\n\n6. Start and enable the mysql service.\n   - Using the service module, I\'ll start the service and set it to enabled.\n\n7. Flush handlers.\n   - I\'ll add a flush_handlers task to ensure tasks are executed in order.\n\n8. Create a my.cnf file in /root/.my.cnf.\n   - Using the file module again, specifying the path and content from the template.\n\n9. Create databases.\n   - I\'ll loop over the mysql_databases list and use the mysql_db module to create each database.\n\n10. List databases.\n    - Using mysql_info to gather info about databases.\n\n11. Import databases.\n    - Again, loop over mysql_databases and check if initial_import is set. Use mysql_db to import each.\n\n12. Create users.\n    - Loop over mysql_users and use mysql_user to create each with their roles.\n\n13. Flush handlers again.\n    - Another flush_handlers task to ensure correct order.\n\nI need to structure each task correctly, ensuring variables are properly templated and conditions are met. Also, I\'ll make sure the playbook is valid YAML and adheres to Ansible\'s standards. Since it\'s for a role, I won\'t include hosts or vars sections, just the tasks.\n\nLet me now translate each step into YAML, making sure the order is correct and all tasks are included without missing any.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml and run it once on localhost\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  host: localhost\n\n- name: Install the mysql package\n  shell: apt-get update && apt-get install -y mysql-server\n  become: true\n\n- name: Configure the mysql server\n  file:\n    path: /etc/mysql/{{ mysql_name }}-server.cnf\n    content: "{{ mysql_server_options | join(\'\\n\') }}"\n    mode: 0644\n\n- name: Configure the mysql client\n  file:\n    path: /etc/mysql/{{ mysql_name }}-client.cnf\n    content: "socket={{ mysql_socket }}"\n    mode: 0644\n\n- name: Initialize the mysql service\n  shell: mysql_initialize_command\n  when: ansible_os_family in [\'Alpine\', \'Archlinux\']\n\n- name: Start and enable the mysql service\n  service:\n    name: mysql\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  flush_handlers:\n\n- name: Create a my.cnf file in the /root/.my.cnf directory\n  file:\n    path: /root/.my.cnf\n    content: "{{ lookup(\'template\', \'my.cnf.j2\') }}"\n    mode: 0600\n\n- name: Create databases\n  community.mysql.mysql_db:\n    name: "{{ db_name }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ mysql_databases }}"\n\n- name: List databases on the target machine\n  community.mysql.mysql_info:\n    state: present\n\n- name: Import databases\n  community.mysql.mysql_db:\n    name: "{{ db_name }}"\n    state: import\n    initial_import: "{{ db_initial_import }}"\n  loop: "{{ mysql_databases | selectattr(\'initial_import\') | list }}"\n\n- name: Create users\n  community.mysql.mysql_user:\n    name: "{{ user }}"\n    password: "{{ password }}"\n    priv: "{{ privileges }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ mysql_users }}"\n\n- name: Flush handlers again\n  flush_handlers:\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T09:06:42.878247831Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 23149052463, 'load_duration': 106779293, 'prompt_eval_count': 791, 'prompt_eval_duration': 486793269, 'eval_count': 1017, 'eval_duration': 22553438515, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--05b9db42-5de6-4eb4-b3d1-d9b2e3573a2b-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 791, 'output_tokens': 1017, 'total_tokens': 1808}
