issions for the directory.\n\nFor Task 2, I'll use the template module, with the src pointing to the template file, dest as /etc/openvpn/client/client.conf. I'll set the owner and group again, probably the same as before. Then, I'll add a notify: openvpn_restart to trigger the restart.\n\nThen, I need to define the handler for openvpn. Using the service module, with name=openvpn, state=restarted, and the handle's name as openvpn_restart.\n\nI should make sure that the playbook starts with '---' and that the YAML is correctly formatted. Also, no extra comments or explanations, just the YAML code.\n\nI think that's the plan. Now, I'll structure the playbook accordingly, ensuring all modules and notifications are correctly placed.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure /etc/openvpn/client directory exists with correct permissions\n  file:\n    path: /etc/openvpn/client\n    state: directory\n    owner: openvpn\n    group: openvpn\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Place client configuration file in the specified directory\n  template:\n    src: client.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/openvpn/client/client.conf\n    owner: openvpn\n    group: openvpn\n    mode: 644\n  notify: openvpn_restart\n\n- name: restart openvpn service\n  service:\n    name: openvpn\n    state: restarted\n  listen: openvpn_restart\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T09:32:01.312680571Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15153899333, 'load_duration': 97783852, 'prompt_eval_count': 293, 'prompt_eval_duration': 81234755, 'eval_count': 740, 'eval_duration': 14974135101, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--482e6c2e-5941-49fd-9018-837b549879f4-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 293, 'output_tokens': 740, 'total_tokens': 1033}
