content='<think>\nAlright, I need to help the user by creating an Ansible Playbook based on their specific instructions. Let me break down what they\'re asking for.\n\nFirst, they mentioned that the playbook must strictly adhere to certain guidelines. It should start with \'---\' on the first line, be valid YAML conforming to yamllint and ansible-lint, and be structured for inclusion in an Ansible Role under the tasks directory. So, I\'ll make sure the structure is correct, without any playbook-level headers like hosts or vars.\n\nThey provided three tasks, each with a description. Let\'s tackle them one by one.\n\nTask 1 is about creating the document root directory for each vhost. I\'ll use the file module with state=directory. The directory name should come from the item in the httpd_vhosts list, so registered_vars.vhost will capture that. The mode is specified as 755, so I\'ll set mode: 0755.\n\nNext, Task 2 involves copying a vhost configuration template. I\'ll use the template module, copying from vhost_conf_template to the Apache config directory. The destination filename should be the vhost name, so dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/{{ vhost.name }}. I\'ll register the result to track if the file was created.\n\nTask 3 is for enabling vhosts on Debian systems using a2ensite. I\'ll use the command module, running a2ensite with the vhost name. I\'ll also include a notify step to reload Apache after enabling the site. The vhost name comes from registered_vars.vhost again.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with a name, action, and the necessary parameters. I\'ll ensure that the tasks are in the correct order and that all variables are correctly referenced. I\'ll also make sure the YAML is properly formatted without any extra comments or explanations, as the user specified.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to ensure it starts with \'---\' and that each task is correctly indented and follows the required structure. This should meet all the user\'s requirements and fit seamlessly into an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the document root directory for each vhost\n  file:\n    path: /var/www/{{ item }}\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n  register: vhost_directories\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Configure the Apache vhost configuration files\n  template:\n    src: vhost_conf_template\n    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/{{ item }}\n    mode: 0644\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n  register: vhost_confs\n  notify: Reload Apache\n\n- name: Enable Apache vhosts on Debian systems\n  command:\n    cmd: /usr/sbin/a2ensite {{ item }}\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n  register: vhost Enables\n  notify: Reload Apache\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T09:57:05.483666612Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12544642180, 'load_duration': 81342539, 'prompt_eval_count': 390, 'prompt_eval_duration': 92377127, 'eval_count': 621, 'eval_duration': 12369446616, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--91f9acb0-4c43-4e47-a64b-828bfb631e37-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 390, 'output_tokens': 621, 'total_tokens': 1011}
_______________________________________Cleaned LLM Output:_______________________________________ 
---
- name: Create the document root directory for each vhost
  file:
    path: /var/www/{{ item }}
    state: directory
    mode: 0755
  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"
  register: vhost_directories
  ignore_errors: yes

- name: Configure the Apache vhost configuration files
  template:
    src: vhost_conf_template
    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/{{ item }}
    mode: 0644
  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"
  register: vhost_confs
  notify: Reload Apache

- name: Enable Apache vhosts on Debian systems
  command:
    cmd: /usr/sbin/a2ensite {{ item }}
  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"
  register: vhost Enables
  notify: Reload Apache


