 each task in order, making sure the YAML is valid and adheres to the role structure.\n\nI think that\'s all. Let me draft the playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the directory for RKE2 manifests\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rke2/manifests\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Copy kube-vip YAML files to the RKE2 manifests directory\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: /etc/rke2/manifests/\n    mode: 0644\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n  loop: "{{ lookup(\'fileglob\', \'templates/kube-vip*.yaml.j2\') | list }}"\n  register: copied_files\n  changed_when: false\n  ignore_errors: yes\n  vars:\n    remote_src: "{{ item | regex_replace(\'.j2\', \'\') }}"\n\n- name: Copy kube-vip load balancer manifests to the RKE2 manifests directory\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: /etc/rke2/manifests/\n    mode: 0644\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n  loop: "{{ lookup(\'fileglob\', \'templates/kube-vip-lb*.yaml.j2\') | list }}"\n  when: rke2_kubevip_cloud_provider_enable\n  register: copied_lb_files\n  changed_when: false\n  ignore_errors: yes\n  vars:\n    remote_src: "{{ item | regex_replace(\'.j2\', \'\') }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T11:24:26.818346295Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13537351896, 'load_duration': 2300169960, 'prompt_eval_count': 401, 'prompt_eval_duration': 321560301, 'eval_count': 788, 'eval_duration': 10914168178, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--8ad6275c-419a-43b6-80b7-e6a5e88c8262-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 401, 'output_tokens': 788, 'total_tokens': 1189}
